# CONCAT is extensible (ed.3 6.6.2.5.3 table 34 / ed.2 2.5.1.5.5 table 29;
# extensible functions ed.3 6.6.1.7.3). It concatenates its string inputs
# in parameter order: 'ab' + 'CD' + 'ef' = 'abCDef'; with 'GH' appended,
# 'abCDefGH'. A nested two-input CONCAT gives the same three-input result.
# All inputs are STRING variables, all results fit the default capacity.
# matiec follows this derivation; STruC++ 72dfcb8 has a variadic overload
# only for IECString values, not the IECStringVar wrappers it generates
# for variables. Its two-input CONCAT overloads accept those wrappers.
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs:
outputs: joined3 joined4 nested
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.6.2.5.3 table 34, 6.6.1.7.3 (extensible functions)
---
0 => joined3='abCDef' joined4='abCDefGH' nested='abCDef'
1 => joined3='abCDef' joined4='abCDefGH' nested='abCDef'
